# Workstation handoff in herdr

The Alis coordinator supports native Claude and OpenCode continuation. Codex and
Antigravity CLI sessions require an explicit summary choice. Cursor has no
registered transfer adapter in this release, including automatic summary transfer.
Never run `--agent cursor`, pass a Cursor conversation ID to another adapter,
copy private agent homes, call hidden lifecycle endpoints, or terminate Cursor.

For this Cursor conversation, explain that automatic transfer is unavailable.
If the user chooses a manual continuation, prepare a short note: task, relevant
constraints, repository/branch and uncommitted work, completed external actions,
exact active Alis operation IDs, and next action. Avoid a long recap. The note
does not transfer files, move live processes, or start a remote agent. Do not
switch agents without the user's choice or claim the laptop is safe to close.

For an existing handoff, check `alis workstation handoff --help`, then use its
exact ID. The CLI must include `open` and `status --watch` for this flow:

- `alis workstation handoff targets --json` lists enrolled SSH destinations.
- `alis workstation handoff status <id> --watch --json` waits for remote acceptance.
- `alis workstation handoff open <id>` opens the continuation in herdr.
- `alis workstation handoff cancel <id> --json` cancels only when requested.

Keep each invocation standalone and read its complete JSON result. For a new
transfer, run the matching handoff skill inside the supported source agent with
the current session ID obtained from its lifecycle context. Never guess a session
ID or select the newest transcript. Select the only eligible destination, or ask
which destination when several qualify. The source must end its turn after
queueing; watch progress in a separate terminal so it can reach a safe boundary.

Herdr groups the product as a space (`alis.os`), service as a tab (`cli.v1`), and
each continuation as a pane. Native continuation uses “Continue where you left
off.” Paired build/Define checkpoints arrive in isolated worktrees. Closing the
browser terminal leaves the remote continuation running.

Keep the laptop awake and connected until `safe_to_close: true`. A queued job,
uploaded archive, created pane, summary, or unreachable destination is not an
acceptance receipt. Normal remote workspace trust and permission prompts apply.
Unknown remote status never permits a duplicate local continuation. Cancellation
releases the source claim only after remote process exit is acknowledged.

Live OS processes are not migrated. Preserve active Alis operation IDs and resume
their monitoring; do not repeat Define, Build, Deploy, or uncertain external
actions. Unknown local background work blocks transfer. Matching CLI, workstation
runtime, agent plugins and destination authentication are required; installing
this Cursor plugin alone does not enable automatic Cursor handoff.
